# scripts/opcount: tn1-lint writes the feature record of N bytes of
# TypeScript (the conformance vectors' sources, repeated); the cost of one
# byte is the slope between the two sizes. The control is the hand Go
# program of the same algorithm (wf10 TS2-COUNT), whose record must be
# byte-equal.
unit byte
sizes 200000 1600000
input go bench/gen {n}
args record {input}
control bench/control
